    {
      "id": "F1",
      "severity": "verified",
      "finding": "Four source SHA256 and Git blob identities match unchanged exact snapshots; protocol and producer hashes match the frozen E303 manifest. Replayed portable packet requires no repository import/network and writes only beside own copy."
    },
    {
      "id": "F2",
      "severity": "verified",
      "finding": "Candidate mean/count/margin recomputed from raw observations for every case. Learned-width evaluation outputs exactly match same-width candidate observations; no scalar width hides the retained score rows. Counts250/200/40 verified."
    },
    {
      "id": "F3",
      "severity": "verified",
      "finding": "Nominal width, occupied vertical raster rows, direct object-normal half-level separation, fitted bilinear edges and nearest-pixel Dev72 channels remain separate. In clean cases the training nominal/raster pairs are30/29,40/39,50/51. Under11degree training rotation,51 is a vertical column count rather than a normal-width claim. Direct half-level crossings use source samp; their scan interpolation is a diagnostic fixture measurement, not fitted uncertainty."
    },
    {
      "id": "F4",
      "severity": "verified",
      "finding": "Training and evaluation are separately allocated deterministic rasters/contexts in producer build calls, sharing numeric source-coordinate conventions. Train fractions yield t=[-36,-18,0,18,33.6], evaluation t=[-43,-11,23,47]; no station t matches. Clean pairs may have identical pixels and global windows overlap in numeric coordinates across separate rasters. Neither separate allocation nor different stations makes a blinded/held-out evaluation; packet marks all outputs EXPOSED."
    },
    {
      "id": "F5",
      "severity": "verified",
      "finding": "Organic-training false-width: mean1/margin1 selects40; ellipse fit39 and gradient72lum/source-px versus clean gradient36. Evaluation true nominal30 has direct/fitted29, constrained learned40 fit null, all four transferred rail/combined scores0. Stronger gradients and strict winner do not qualify training provenance."
    },
    {
      "id": "F6",
      "severity": "verified",
      "finding": "Reverse clean30-to-organic ellipse: four evaluation stations have left/right rails, inner channels and combined score1; free/constrained edge fit29 with gradient72. Bilateral consistency therefore does not establish renderer/path identity."
    },
    {
      "id": "F7",
      "severity": "verified",
      "finding": "Local widening retains nominal46/direct-fit45 while learned30 constrained fit is null and source channels0. Offset4 case retains direct object-normal29 before caller-origin shift but default latLim3 free/constrained fits null and channels0. These are distinct fixture mechanisms, not proof of ribbon absence."
    },
    {
      "id": "F8",
      "severity": "verified",
      "finding": "All-hidden training returns legacy20 with all candidate counts0 and explicit -Infinity tags; zero-lift returns20 with five visible samples per width but tied scores0. Diagnostic states abstain and every calibratedWidthPx is null."
    },
    {
      "id": "F9",
      "severity": "verified",
      "finding": "Frozen rails-occluded prediction failed as reported. Rail boxes y108..119 and137..148 also contain guard sample rows108/148 at nominalW30, preventing ground estimation. Rail, inner and combined outputs are null at all four evaluation stations. Negative prediction remains in result without tuning geometry/masks after observation."
    }
